  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\n\nAfter showers clear Wednesday morning, it should be a nice day as \nsfc high pressure moves over much of the Northern Plains. Highs warm \nto the low to mid 80s.\n\nModel guidance shows the H5 ridge retrograding a bit to the west and \namplifying as we head into the weekend. That will place us in \nnorthwesterly flow for much of the extended and allow more series of \nwaves to traverse the flow and impact the area. As such, should see \ncontinued chances for showers and storms. At this time, the best \nchances appear to be late Friday into Saturday morning, and late \nSunday into Monday, but even then these chances remain low at \n15 to 30%. In addition, will see highs steadily climb to the \nupper 80s/low 90s by Saturday and Sunday.",
